{"title":"The Best Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: What to Get Your Favorite Gravel Biker","link":"https://bikerumor.com/best-gifts-for-gravel-cyclists/","date":1793984400000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/2026-Bikerumor-Gravel-Gift-Guide_Tenerife-header-1536x1024.jpg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1024\" alt=\"2026 Bikerumor Gravel Gift Guide: Cory riding gravel in Tenerife\" /></p>\n<p>On the hunt for the best gifts for the gravel riders on your holiday shopping list? Cyclists, in general, are tricky to buy for, and gravel bike riders can be especially tricky. It’s still kind of a new-ish discipline. And a lot of riders are still figuring out what gravel means to them.Are they a serious racer, a weekend doddler, an all-terrain explorer, or maybe even the kind of adventurer that heads out on week-long, self-supported bikepacking trips? </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Any way they ride gravel, we can help find that perfect gift to put a smile on the face of your favorite gravel bike rider.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Ride Gravel For Less</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Buy-your-favorite-gravel-rider-an-affordable-new-carbon-Ari-Shafer-gravel-bike.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Buy-your-favorite-gravel-rider-an-affordable-new-carbon-Ari-Shafer-gravel-bike.jpg\" alt=\"2026 Bikerumor Gravel Gift Guide: Buy your favorite gravel cyclists a new bike from Ari\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Buy-your-favorite-gravel-rider-an-affordable-new-carbon-Ari-Shafer-gravel-bike.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Buy-your-favorite-gravel-rider-an-affordable-new-carbon-Ari-Shafer-gravel-bike-297x178.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Buy-your-favorite-gravel-rider-an-affordable-new-carbon-Ari-Shafer-gravel-bike-1536x922.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Buy-your-favorite-gravel-rider-an-affordable-new-carbon-Ari-Shafer-gravel-bike-120x72.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Buy-your-favorite-gravel-rider-an-affordable-new-carbon-Ari-Shafer-gravel-bike-768x461.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Buy-your-favorite-gravel-rider-an-affordable-new-carbon-Ari-Shafer-gravel-bike-1500x900.jpg 1500w\" /></a><figcaption><i>(all photos © individual manufacturers)</i></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Adding a complete carbon gravel bike to a gift guide sounds a bit over-the-top, right! Who has the gifting budget for that, after all? But hear us out, the carbon <strong>Ari Shafer</strong> ticks pretty much all the gravel boxes – from weekend rides to week-long adventures. And it promises solid affordability. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>You get a lightweight and aero-optimized carbon frame, monster tire clearance up to 700x58mm or 29×2.25″, fully integrated routing, bikepacking-ready mounts &amp; internal storage, and versatile all-terrain geometry. It’s a confident all-rounder. But it still won’t break the bank. “<em>Flagship performance without the flagship price.</em>”  </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ari-Shafer-Sport-affordable-carbon-gravel-bike-with-SHimano-Cues-11sp-drivetrain.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1350\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ari-Shafer-Sport-affordable-carbon-gravel-bike-with-SHimano-Cues-11sp-drivetrain.jpg\" alt=\"Ari Shafer affordable $2550 carbon gravel bike with Shimano Cues 1x11\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ari-Shafer-Sport-affordable-carbon-gravel-bike-with-SHimano-Cues-11sp-drivetrain.jpg 2400w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ari-Shafer-Sport-affordable-carbon-gravel-bike-with-SHimano-Cues-11sp-drivetrain-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ari-Shafer-Sport-affordable-carbon-gravel-bike-with-SHimano-Cues-11sp-drivetrain-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ari-Shafer-Sport-affordable-carbon-gravel-bike-with-SHimano-Cues-11sp-drivetrain-120x68.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ari-Shafer-Sport-affordable-carbon-gravel-bike-with-SHimano-Cues-11sp-drivetrain-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ari-Shafer-Sport-affordable-carbon-gravel-bike-with-SHimano-Cues-11sp-drivetrain-2048x1152.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ari-Shafer-Sport-affordable-carbon-gravel-bike-with-SHimano-Cues-11sp-drivetrain-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ari-Shafer-Sport-affordable-carbon-gravel-bike-with-SHimano-Cues-11sp-drivetrain-1600x900.jpg 1600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Framesets are available from just €2000, complete bikes from just $2550 (direct from <a href=\"https://i-rn.fr/4e9aRUl\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Ari Bikes</strong></a>). You can even save an extra two to three hundred bucks off a complete build now in Ari’s Black Friday deals. Or a hundred buckaroos off the frameset-only option. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Get-more-people-on-gravel-bikes-with-affordable-Ari-Shafer.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Get-more-people-on-gravel-bikes-with-affordable-Ari-Shafer.jpg\" alt=\"2026 Bikerumor Gravel Gift Guide: get more riders on gravel with affordable Ari bikes\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Get-more-people-on-gravel-bikes-with-affordable-Ari-Shafer.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Get-more-people-on-gravel-bikes-with-affordable-Ari-Shafer-297x178.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Get-more-people-on-gravel-bikes-with-affordable-Ari-Shafer-1536x922.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Get-more-people-on-gravel-bikes-with-affordable-Ari-Shafer-120x72.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Get-more-people-on-gravel-bikes-with-affordable-Ari-Shafer-768x461.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Get-more-people-on-gravel-bikes-with-affordable-Ari-Shafer-1500x900.jpg 1500w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Think your favorite gravel would prefer a pedal-assist version? Then, check out the <strong>Shafer HP</strong> ebike powered by the excellent and natural-feeling TQ HPR60 motor. </p>\n\n\n\n<p><em>Sponsored Placement</em></p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Essentials At Your Fingertips</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Apidura-Racing-Bolt-On-Top-Tube-Pack-1L-bikepacking-bag-on-bike.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1500\" height=\"844\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Apidura-Racing-Bolt-On-Top-Tube-Pack-1L-bikepacking-bag-on-bike.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: Essentials at your bikepacking-ready fingertips Apidura 1L Racing Bolt-On Top Tube Pack\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Apidura-Racing-Bolt-On-Top-Tube-Pack-1L-bikepacking-bag-on-bike.jpg 1500w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Apidura-Racing-Bolt-On-Top-Tube-Pack-1L-bikepacking-bag-on-bike-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Apidura-Racing-Bolt-On-Top-Tube-Pack-1L-bikepacking-bag-on-bike-120x68.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Apidura-Racing-Bolt-On-Top-Tube-Pack-1L-bikepacking-bag-on-bike-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Apidura-Racing-Bolt-On-Top-Tube-Pack-1L-bikepacking-bag-on-bike-1200x675.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Nothing beats a toptube bag for keeping your snacks and essential electronics close at hand. Perennial favorites are those that naturally keep water out, are almost self-closing, and can be easily opened and secured shut with one hand, even while riding over rough terrain. Our first pick is an OG on the fast-packing scene in the <strong>1L Apidura Racing Top Tube Bag</strong> with the magnetic clasp on its flap top. Pick the bolt-on version (on sale at $80 from <a href=\"https://backcountry.tnu8.net/c/2227671/358742/5311?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.backcountry.com%2Fapidura-racing-bolt-on-top-tube-pack\" target=\"_blank\">Backcountry</a>) if your buddy’s bike is new enough to have bolts on its toptube, or the strap-on version (66€ from <a href=\"https://www.apidura.com/shop/racing-top-tube-pack/\" target=\"_blank\">Apidura</a>, or $84 at that Backcountry link) to fit almost any bike.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Tailfin-Top-Tube-Bag-Flip-small-1-1L-bikepacking-bag.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1500\" height=\"844\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Tailfin-Top-Tube-Bag-Flip-small-1-1L-bikepacking-bag.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: Essentials at your bikepacking-ready fingertips Tailfin 1.1L Top Tube Bag - Flip\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Tailfin-Top-Tube-Bag-Flip-small-1-1L-bikepacking-bag.jpg 1500w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Tailfin-Top-Tube-Bag-Flip-small-1-1L-bikepacking-bag-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Tailfin-Top-Tube-Bag-Flip-small-1-1L-bikepacking-bag-120x68.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Tailfin-Top-Tube-Bag-Flip-small-1-1L-bikepacking-bag-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Tailfin-Top-Tube-Bag-Flip-small-1-1L-bikepacking-bag-1200x675.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Our second pick is the newer but similarly-shaped <strong>1.1L Tailfin Top Tube Tube Bag Flip</strong> (85€ directly from <a href=\"https://www.tailfin.cc/product/top-tube-cockpit/top-tube-bag-flip/?v=9c049173fad5\" target=\"_blank\">Tailfin</a>), which features a versatile mounting setup with or without bolts on the bike’s toptube. Either option is big enough to carry a smartphone, compact camera, or plenty of snacks. And having one can free your gravel grinding lifestyle from the need to wear a traditional cycling jersey with pockets. Strap a top tube bag on, and enjoy the freedom of riding in your favorite t-shirt.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Haul All Your Gear</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Handlebar-Pack-QR_quick-release-install-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-handlebar-bag_now-in-dark-sand.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1200\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Handlebar-Pack-QR_quick-release-install-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-handlebar-bag_now-in-dark-sand.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: Haul all your bikepacking gear with Ortlieb Handlebar-Pack QR\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Handlebar-Pack-QR_quick-release-install-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-handlebar-bag_now-in-dark-sand.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Handlebar-Pack-QR_quick-release-install-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-handlebar-bag_now-in-dark-sand-297x178.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Handlebar-Pack-QR_quick-release-install-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-handlebar-bag_now-in-dark-sand-1536x922.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Handlebar-Pack-QR_quick-release-install-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-handlebar-bag_now-in-dark-sand-120x72.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Handlebar-Pack-QR_quick-release-install-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-handlebar-bag_now-in-dark-sand-768x461.jpg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Gravel and bikepacking go hand in hand, so it’s always important to be able to strap a few days’ worth of gear onto your gravel bike to head out on an adventure. But even if credit card fast-packing is more your (your favorite graveler’s) speed, you still want to have trusty packs to keep your gear safe. Nothing beats Ortlieb’s made-in-Germany Waterproof Guarantee. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>We especially love the easy-to-attach and expandable <strong>Ortlieb Handlebar Pack QR</strong> (on sale for $181 via <a href=\"https://backcountry.tnu8.net/c/2227671/358742/5311?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.backcountry.com%2Fortlieb-handlebar-pack-qr\" target=\"_blank\">Backcountry</a>) for its handy bar mount and easy packing.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Seat-Pack-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-saddlebag_now-in-dark-sand.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1333\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Seat-Pack-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-saddlebag_now-in-dark-sand.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: Haul all your bikepacking gear with Ortlieb mid-sized 11L Seat-Pack\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Seat-Pack-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-saddlebag_now-in-dark-sand.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Seat-Pack-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-saddlebag_now-in-dark-sand-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Seat-Pack-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-saddlebag_now-in-dark-sand-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Seat-Pack-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-saddlebag_now-in-dark-sand-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Seat-Pack-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-saddlebag_now-in-dark-sand-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Seat-Pack-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-saddlebag_now-in-dark-sand-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ortlieb-Seat-Pack-11L-waterproof-bikepacking-saddlebag_now-in-dark-sand-720x480.jpg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>And their mid-sized <strong>11L Seat-Pack</strong> ($190 at <a href=\"https://rei.pxf.io/c/2227671/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F188016%2Fortlieb-seat-pack-saddle-bag-11-liters\" target=\"_blank\">REI</a>) offers plenty of adjustable storage in a classic, easy-to-mount bikepacking saddlebag design. Pair the two together, in original black or new dark sand, and you’d be ready for everything from a backcountry overnighter to a week-long adventure tour.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Cover Your Butt</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ass-Savers-Win-Wing-2-Gravel-strap-on-rear-fender.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1067\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ass-Savers-Win-Wing-2-Gravel-strap-on-rear-fender.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: Cover your butt with an Ass Savers Win Wing 2 Gravel fender\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ass-Savers-Win-Wing-2-Gravel-strap-on-rear-fender.jpg 1600w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ass-Savers-Win-Wing-2-Gravel-strap-on-rear-fender-297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ass-Savers-Win-Wing-2-Gravel-strap-on-rear-fender-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ass-Savers-Win-Wing-2-Gravel-strap-on-rear-fender-120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ass-Savers-Win-Wing-2-Gravel-strap-on-rear-fender-768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ass-Savers-Win-Wing-2-Gravel-strap-on-rear-fender-800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Ass-Savers-Win-Wing-2-Gravel-strap-on-rear-fender-720x480.jpg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Riding gravel means getting dirty on drop bars. But that doesn’t mean that your butt needs to get wet and dirty, too. Ass Savers has your rear in mind with their simple, lightweight but effective <strong>Win Wing 2 Gravel</strong> fender (27-29€ from <a href=\"https://ass-savers.com/collections/win-wing\" target=\"_blank\">Ass Savers</a>). The wishbone bracket straps onto virtually any bike’s seatstays in seconds, and can be topped with various fender blade designs to show off a little style while taming rear wheel spray. We’re partial to the low-key look, but feel free to express yourself when buying presents for your special gravel someone. I even like to ride one under a big bikepacking saddlepack to keep things cleaner, while getting gear in and out. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Bumbinos-Splash-Pack-strap-on-Kids-bike-gravel-fenders.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2400\" height=\"1350\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Bumbinos-Splash-Pack-strap-on-Kids-bike-gravel-fenders.jpg\" alt=\"Bumbinos Splash Pack strap-on Kids bike gravel fenders in cool, colorful designs\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Bumbinos-Splash-Pack-strap-on-Kids-bike-gravel-fenders.jpg 2400w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Bumbinos-Splash-Pack-strap-on-Kids-bike-gravel-fenders-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Bumbinos-Splash-Pack-strap-on-Kids-bike-gravel-fenders-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Bumbinos-Splash-Pack-strap-on-Kids-bike-gravel-fenders-120x68.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Bumbinos-Splash-Pack-strap-on-Kids-bike-gravel-fenders-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Bumbinos-Splash-Pack-strap-on-Kids-bike-gravel-fenders-2048x1152.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Bumbinos-Splash-Pack-strap-on-Kids-bike-gravel-fenders-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Bumbinos-Splash-Pack-strap-on-Kids-bike-gravel-fenders-1600x900.jpg 1600w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>While you’re at it, does your kid ride gravel, too? But they don’t need something with ass written on it, right? Well, sister brand Bumbinos has kid’s bums protected from mud &amp; rain, too. Bumbinos are kid bike-sized for 14-16″ or 18-20″ wheels, and come in way more fun designs than Ass Savers ever imagined. A Splash Pack (35€ from <a href=\"https://bumbinos.com/collections/splash-packs-full-mudguard-sets\" target=\"_blank\">Bumbinos</a>) includes matching front &amp; rear fenders, plus cool stickers.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Ready When the Lights Go Out, In More Ways Than One</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exposure-Zenith-4-premium-high-power-helmet-mounted-cycling-headlight.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1125\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exposure-Zenith-4-premium-high-power-helmet-mounted-cycling-headlight.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: Ready to ride at night with Exposure Zenith 4 headlight\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exposure-Zenith-4-premium-high-power-helmet-mounted-cycling-headlight.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exposure-Zenith-4-premium-high-power-helmet-mounted-cycling-headlight-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exposure-Zenith-4-premium-high-power-helmet-mounted-cycling-headlight-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exposure-Zenith-4-premium-high-power-helmet-mounted-cycling-headlight-120x68.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exposure-Zenith-4-premium-high-power-helmet-mounted-cycling-headlight-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Exposure-Zenith-4-premium-high-power-helmet-mounted-cycling-headlight-1200x675.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>When it gets dark, the riding doesn’t have to stop. We love a simple bike light to keep the fun going after the sun goes down. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are looking for versatile on- and off-road-ready lighting, we love the 2360 lumen output of Exposure’s top-tier <strong>Zenith 4</strong> headlight ($305 direct from <a href=\"https://www.exposurelights.com/products/zenith-4\" target=\"_blank\">Exposure</a>). Jeremy <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/exposure-six-pack-15-and-zenith-4-review-the-best-mountain-bike-lights-money-can-buy/\" target=\"_blank\">reviewed this bright light</a> mounted to his helmet. But it also comes with a bar mount, making it versatile for all types of off-road riding, and a sound all-around bike light investment.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/extra-SRAM-AXS-battery-spare.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1000\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/extra-SRAM-AXS-battery-spare.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: Be prepared with a spare SRAM AXS battery\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/extra-SRAM-AXS-battery-spare.jpg 2000w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/extra-SRAM-AXS-battery-spare-297x149.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/extra-SRAM-AXS-battery-spare-1536x768.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/extra-SRAM-AXS-battery-spare-120x60.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/extra-SRAM-AXS-battery-spare-768x384.jpg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>If your gravel-riding loved one rides a bike with a wireless electronic SRAM drivetrain, they’ve invariably run out of juice, out on a ride. A spare <strong>AXS battery</strong> (on sale now, $58 at <a href=\"https://backcountry.tnu8.net/c/2227671/358742/5311?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.backcountry.com%2Fsram-red-etap-battery\" target=\"_blank\">Backcountry</a>) is the perfect insurance policy to not get caught out with a bike that no longer shifts. They’ll keep it charged and ready at home, and pack it in their bags for any longer trip. And they will thank you the next time the battery on their bike runs out!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Be Ready For Failure, Too</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/WTB-NanoAir-TPU-tan-gravel-bike-inner-tube.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"900\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/WTB-NanoAir-TPU-tan-gravel-bike-inner-tube.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: Be ready for tire failure with a WTB NanoAir TPU spare inner tube\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/WTB-NanoAir-TPU-tan-gravel-bike-inner-tube.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/WTB-NanoAir-TPU-tan-gravel-bike-inner-tube-297x223.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/WTB-NanoAir-TPU-tan-gravel-bike-inner-tube-120x90.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/WTB-NanoAir-TPU-tan-gravel-bike-inner-tube-768x576.jpg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Well, at least be ready for a flat tire. Every rider of every type of bike should be prepared to fix a flat. Carrying spare tubes used to be bulky and kinda heavy. But no longer with fancy, light TPU tubes that pack down small. There are a lot of brands and fun colors out there. The trick for gravel is to get the right size – width, and valve length. Most of the time, you’ll be good with the standard 32-47mm width &amp; 48mm long valve from tubes like the brown <strong>WTB NanoAir TPU</strong> gravel tube ($25 at <a href=\"https://rei.pxf.io/c/2227671/1448521/17195?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.rei.com%2Fproduct%2F234820%2Fwtb-nanoair-tpu-presta-tube-700c\" target=\"_blank\">REI</a>).</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/lightweight-TPU-gravel-bike-inner-tubes-rainbow_milKit_Panaracer_Pirelli_Tubolito_Schwalbe_Continental.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2464\" height=\"1155\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/lightweight-TPU-gravel-bike-inner-tubes-rainbow_milKit_Panaracer_Pirelli_Tubolito_Schwalbe_Continental.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: Be prepared with TPU inner tubes from MilKit Panaracer, Pirelli, Tubolito, Schwalbe &amp; Continental\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/lightweight-TPU-gravel-bike-inner-tubes-rainbow_milKit_Panaracer_Pirelli_Tubolito_Schwalbe_Continental.jpg 2464w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/lightweight-TPU-gravel-bike-inner-tubes-rainbow_milKit_Panaracer_Pirelli_Tubolito_Schwalbe_Continental-297x139.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/lightweight-TPU-gravel-bike-inner-tubes-rainbow_milKit_Panaracer_Pirelli_Tubolito_Schwalbe_Continental-1536x720.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/lightweight-TPU-gravel-bike-inner-tubes-rainbow_milKit_Panaracer_Pirelli_Tubolito_Schwalbe_Continental-120x56.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/lightweight-TPU-gravel-bike-inner-tubes-rainbow_milKit_Panaracer_Pirelli_Tubolito_Schwalbe_Continental-768x360.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/lightweight-TPU-gravel-bike-inner-tubes-rainbow_milKit_Panaracer_Pirelli_Tubolito_Schwalbe_Continental-2048x960.jpg 2048w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>But there’s a full rainbow of more good TPU options, like the blue <strong>MilKit TPU Road &amp; Gravel</strong>, <strong>Panaracer Purple Lite</strong>, yellow <strong>Pirelli Cinturato Smarttube</strong> ($42 at <a href=\"https://backcountry.tnu8.net/c/2227671/358742/5311?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.backcountry.com%2Fpirelli-cinturato-smartube-pir1wvi\" target=\"_blank\">Backcountry</a>), orange <strong>Tubolito S-CX/Gravel</strong>, or transparent white <strong>Schwalbe Aerothan</strong> or <strong>Continental ContiTPU. All are great options, really. Before you hit buy, first maybe double-check</strong> if your friend’s gravel bike has deep aero wheels (which would need longer valves) or giant &gt;2″ MTB-sized tires (which would mean 29″ MTB size TPU tubes).</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Stay Hydrated Out There</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Zefal-Magnum-Pro-high-capacity-cycling-water-bottle.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"650\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Zefal-Magnum-Pro-high-capacity-cycling-water-bottle.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: stay hydrated with Zéfal Magnum Pro high capacity water bottles\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Zefal-Magnum-Pro-high-capacity-cycling-water-bottle.jpg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Zefal-Magnum-Pro-high-capacity-cycling-water-bottle-297x161.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Zefal-Magnum-Pro-high-capacity-cycling-water-bottle-120x65.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Zefal-Magnum-Pro-high-capacity-cycling-water-bottle-768x416.jpg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The core of our being, cyclists need water to pedal. And big gravel adventures can only keep going if you stay well hydrated. The ultra-distance bikepacker’s secret weapon is the almost 1L made-in-France <strong>Zéfal Magnum Pro</strong> high capacity 975ml/33oz water bottle that fits in standard bottle cages (11€ from <a href=\"https://www.zefal.com/en/bottles/729-706-magnum-pro.html#/98-couleur-smocked_black\" target=\"_blank\">Zefal</a> direct). No other bike bottle is as trusted by those serious gravel cyclists who venture far off the beaten track. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Evoc-Hydro-Pro-3.jpeg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1029\" height=\"686\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Evoc-Hydro-Pro-3.jpeg\" alt=\"studio image of the Evoc Hydro Pro 3 hydration vest.\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Evoc-Hydro-Pro-3.jpeg 1029w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Evoc-Hydro-Pro-3-297x198.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Evoc-Hydro-Pro-3-120x80.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Evoc-Hydro-Pro-3-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Evoc-Hydro-Pro-3-800x533.jpeg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Evoc-Hydro-Pro-3-720x480.jpeg 720w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are looking to haul more than a couple of big bottles, bike hydration vests have become a popular off-road biking option. In our comprehensive <em>Best Of</em>… series, we faced off with 8 of the <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/best-cycling-hydration-vests/\" target=\"_blank\">best cycling hydration vest</a> offerings, comparing and contrasting their best attributes. One of our favorites is this <strong>EVOC Hydro Pro 3L</strong> pack ($140 on sale now at <a href=\"https://backcountry.tnu8.net/c/2227671/358742/5311?subId3=bw-fdd34090-67e1[[[6bedc3[&amp;u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.backcountry.com%2Fevoc-hydro-pro-hydration-3l-backpack\" target=\"_blank\">Backcountry</a>) for its light and effective water &amp; snacks carrying capacity.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Stay Safe On The Road</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Wahoo-TRACKR-RADAR-linked-to-ELEMNT-ROAM-cycling-computer.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1500\" height=\"820\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Wahoo-TRACKR-RADAR-linked-to-ELEMNT-ROAM-cycling-computer.jpg\" alt=\"Gifts for Gravel Cyclists: Stay Safe On The Road Wahoo Trackr Radar\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Wahoo-TRACKR-RADAR-linked-to-ELEMNT-ROAM-cycling-computer.jpg 1500w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Wahoo-TRACKR-RADAR-linked-to-ELEMNT-ROAM-cycling-computer-297x162.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Wahoo-TRACKR-RADAR-linked-to-ELEMNT-ROAM-cycling-computer-120x66.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Wahoo-TRACKR-RADAR-linked-to-ELEMNT-ROAM-cycling-computer-768x420.jpg 768w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>We gravelers may dream of car-free riding everywhere we roam, but the truth of the matter is that we often ride on asphalt in between gravel bits. On those sections sharing the road with traffic, a smart light that combines visibility with radar to warn of approaching cars is hard to beat. There are more and more cycling radar taillight solutions on the market these days. But our choice for gravel riders is the <strong>Wahoo Trackr Radar</strong> ($250 at <a href=\"https://backcountry.tnu8.net/c/2227671/358742/5311?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.backcountry.com%2Fwahoo-fitness-trackr-radar\" target=\"_blank\">Backcountry</a>), as it can be set to low light output levels and a battery extender mode that won’t irritate your riding buddies with regular flashing. But it still gets bright when it detects an approaching car and has real-world run times up to 20 hours to keep you alert on even the longest rides. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>Plus, it pairs seamlessly with the latest Roam 3 in our <em><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/cycling-holiday-gift-guide-best-gifts-cyclists/\" target=\"_blank\">Best Gifts For Cyclists</a></em> guide, as well as the Ace &amp; Bolt, too.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Support The Local Bike Shop</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/Bike-Shop-Status-during-COVID-19-pandemic_an-interactive-map_Is-your-local-bike-shop-open.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1455\" height=\"818\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Bike-Shop-Status-during-COVID-19-pandemic_an-interactive-map_Is-your-local-bike-shop-open-edited.jpg\" alt=\"Bike Shop Status during COVID-19 pandemic: an interactive map\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Bike-Shop-Status-during-COVID-19-pandemic_an-interactive-map_Is-your-local-bike-shop-open-edited.jpg 1455w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Bike-Shop-Status-during-COVID-19-pandemic_an-interactive-map_Is-your-local-bike-shop-open-edited-297x167.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Bike-Shop-Status-during-COVID-19-pandemic_an-interactive-map_Is-your-local-bike-shop-open-edited-120x67.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Bike-Shop-Status-during-COVID-19-pandemic_an-interactive-map_Is-your-local-bike-shop-open-edited-768x432.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Bike-Shop-Status-during-COVID-19-pandemic_an-interactive-map_Is-your-local-bike-shop-open-edited-1200x675.jpg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>We can’t say it enough. But when in doubt, pop into the local bikeshop nearest to the gravel cyclists on your gift list and get them a <em><strong>Gift Certificate</strong></em>. Almost everything above can be sourced through that local shop. And all shops are happy to get you a gift certificate suited to your gifting budget. Then, when the time comes for regular maintenance or to replace something that’s simply worn out, the local bikeshop is always a great place to start. Everyone loves a gift certificate from somewhere they actually want to shop. You can even be sneaky and ask your special gravel cyclist to recommend which bike shop they think is best in town, if you want to be sure to support the right one.</p>\n\n\n\n<p></p>","author":"Cory Benson","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/best-gifts-for-gravel-cyclists/#comments","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"8130df81050a6f97a3a31bad436e2f290ccb5c0c3649027e0cbc4438646557d6","category":"Cycling"}